# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as LF on
# every platform, Windows included. Without this file Git for Windows applies
# its own core.autocrlf default, which can make an entire checkout show up as
# modified on a build machine -- noise that a re-clone does NOT fix, because the
# setting reproduces it. VS Code handles LF files on Windows natively.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
